Fixed in `tokio-stream/src/stream_map.rs:687`:

```rust
fn size_hint(&self) -> (usize, Option<usize>) {
    let mut ret: (usize, Option<usize>) = (0, Some(0));

    for (_, stream) in &self.entries {
        let hint = stream.size_hint();

        ret.0 = ret.0.saturating_add(hint.0);

        match (ret.1, hint.1) {
            (Some(a), Some(b)) => ret.1 = a.checked_add(b),
            (Some(_), None) => ret.1 = None,
            _ => {}
        }
    }

    ret
}
```

- Lower bound uses `saturating_add`, so it clamps at `usize::MAX` — the strongest lower bound expressible.
- Upper bound uses `checked_add`, collapsing to `None` (unknown/unbounded) when the sum can't be represented, which is the correct conservative upper bound.
- The explicit `(usize, Option<usize>)` annotation is needed because the integer literals were previously only pinned by the `+=`/`+` operations; without it the method calls hit `E0689` on an ambiguous numeric type.

`size_hint_overflow` now passes, and the whole `tokio-stream` suite is green (28 passing in `stream_stream_map`, no failures elsewhere).
